# ── .env.example ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Names of the build-time values Money Scribe reads, without their values.
# Copy this file to .env and fill it in locally; .env is gitignored and must
# never be committed.
#
# Money Scribe talks to no backend yet (the provider is not chosen), so it
# needs no keys yet. Add a line here (name only) whenever a build-time value is
# introduced, for example a server URL or a public client key. Server secrets
# never belong in the app.
#
# Values are passed at build time, never bundled as an asset:
#   flutter run --dart-define-from-file=.env
# and read in Dart as compile-time constants:
#   const value = String.fromEnvironment('NAME');
#
# In CI, store real values as environment secrets (see docs/github-setup.md,
# section 3), never in the repository.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
